What are the benefits of children playing with foam puzzle mats
First of all, what are the benefits of children playing with foam puzzle mats
Train children to understand the relationship between “parts” and “wholes” – let children know that many “parts” can be pieced together into a “whole”, and “all” is composed of “many parts”.
Cultivate the concept of plane combination in children – building blocks are three-dimensional combination, and puzzle is the concept of plane combination, spelling out an object and a logical thing in a limited 2D range.
Train children to learn the meaning of sequence/sequence/logic – many children know to start from the edge when they first come into contact with multiple puzzles. This is the meaning of learning order, order, and logic, and learning classification from observation and judgment.
Learn problem-solving methods and strategies – Playing jigsaw puzzles can learn the ability to reason and think, as children will try different options and come down to the right one, that is, through the process of assumption, judgment, and choice, let the child He learned how to solve problems with logic.
Improve children’s frustration tolerance and endurance – children will inevitably make mistakes when playing puzzles. At this time, they will feel very lost and express their willingness not to play, but adults can help them and help them through the difficulties.
Get affirmation from the chaos/destruction reconstruction and build confidence in yourself – when the child completes the puzzle, it is easy for him to have a sense of accomplishment, which is very important to improve the child’s interest, and it is also his self-confidence to complete the puzzle independently in the future source.
