Anyone who needs to ship something big — or a great deal of something small — rents what is known as an intermodal container for the purpose. But that’s not an easy task at the moment — there simply aren’t enough transport boxes available.
Anyone in Europe seeking to buy one can only get it secondhand: Even new containers are first loaded with goods in China and used for one shipment before they can be taken possession of here.
