Why does the blind rivet break the nail core rather than at the breakpoint of the pull nail?
The tension of the nail core itself is not stable, the breaking point force is very close to the tension of the nail core itself, or the heat treatment is not done well, and the nail core is brittle.
The first pull riveting has caused damage to the nail core, so that the tension at the damaged part is less than the breaking point force. When pulling again for the second time, the nail core will break from the injured part.
