C5 definition method — division of dry and wet gas
Wet gas: refers to the natural gas with the content of hydrocarbon liquid above C5 higher than 13.5 cubic centimeter in 1 standard cubic meter of natural gas.
Lean gas: refers to the natural gas with hydrocarbon liquid content above C3 less than 94 cubic centimeter in 1 standard cubic meter of natural gas.
