Today there are many diets to lose weight, some are not healthy and totally harmful to health and others on the contrary help you lose weight in an effective and healthy way. This time I'm going to talk to you about the alkaline diet, which defends that many of the diseases that occur today are due to poor diet and high levels of acidity that is in the body.
5 Disadvantages of the alkaline diet
7 Other elements that help balance the pH in the blood The pH level in the body
A good diet is essential to have good pH levels and thus avoid the appearance of different diseases. The alkaline diet seeks that the pH in the blood is adequate and promises for this weight loss, good bone health and the prevention of different diseases caused by a high degree of acidity.
It is a diet that encourages healthy eating based on such nutritious foods as fruit, vegetables or nuts. In addition to this, it prohibits the intake of fats, alcohol or sugar.
Other advantages of the alkaline diet is the prevention of possible diseases such as arthritis, increases energy in the body or helps reduce the level of anxiety in the person.
As with most diets, before starting the alkaline diet it is advisable to go to a nutritionist to assess whether it is a regime worth following or is it better to start with another type of diet. The doctor you will need to do some tests to check your pH level in the blood and know if you need the intake of acidic and alkaline foods.
Those who defend the alkaline diet, promote that the pH balance makes the memory improve enormously, that the body has much more energy and that sleep quality is much higher. However, it is a type of diet that you cannot start on your own since it is advisable to first go to a nutritionist who will review you and tell you if it is worth starting such a diet.
