A flaw in the Twitter application allowed, until a few months ago, to access locked accounts bypassing the locking mechanism implemented by the IT giant.
In order to unlock the account, the owner needs to confirm his identity by providing some information, such as the email address and the phone number.
“I recently found a flaw in the lockout mechanism Twitter has in place to protect accounts from unauthorized access. This flaw resulted in a complete bypass of the verification page which is presented to users if their account is locked.” reads the post published by the expert.
In order to complete the bypass procedure, the attacker needs to retrieve the information to unlock it. In order to achieve his goal, expertused the iOS Twitter app to access the account’s settings and get the email address and phone number of the legitimate owner of the account.
“The settings option for Twitter (which allows you to add/remove Twitter accounts) is present on your phone even if you’ve never installed the Twitter app before. “I was able to add my locked Twitter account to my device through settings without any problems.”
“I was then able to submit this information on the verification page I was previously displayed, which allowed me tologinto the desktop Twitter site as well. The locked flag was then completely removed from my account.” wrote the expert.
Twitter launched a bounty program in 2014, it is run on the HackerOne platform and bug hunters could earn up to $15,000 for most severe issues.
